.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
creates and tracks collections of sprites 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
.SS "Events"
Things that happen to a sprite that might require intervention, such as collisions, completed animations, going offscreen, etc\&.\&.\&. will generate events\&. Events generated by sprites first go to any handlers attached directly to the \fBSprite\fP, then propagate up to the \fBSpriteLayer\fP and then the \fBEventManager\fP until they are handled\&.

.PP
Things that happen to a sprite layer go to the layer's handlers first, then propagate to the \fBEventManager\fP's handlers if they weren't handled by the layer\&. 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "addParticle (\fBParticle\fP value)"

.PP
Add a live detached particle\&. Rejects expired particles, particles owned by another layer and a full budget\&. Adding a particle already in this layer is harmless\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP Object to add/remove; JavaScript parameter is named value\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
ParticleEffects 
.RE
.PP

.SS "addSprite (\fBSprite\fP newSprite)"

.PP
Add a \fBSprite\fP and its mounted descendants to this layer\&. Transfers the group from its previous layer when necessary, preserving its layer-coordinate transforms and mounting relationships\&. Inserts the host first, followed by descendants, in front of existing sprites\&. A \fBSprite\fP already in this layer is unchanged\&. Use \fBSprite::moveBehind()\fP or \fBSprite::moveInFrontOf()\fP to change one member's draw order\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fInewSprite\fP The \fBSprite\fP to add\&. An attached child must first be detached with \fBPart::detachSprite()\fP; otherwise the call throws without changing either layer\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Transfer must occur outside animation modifiers and locked physics callbacks\&. Root constraints and physical animation rigs are disconnected on removal; ordinary Parts, artwork and modifiers remain associated\&. Imported Spriter sprites retain their shared model and artwork independently of the source layer\&. Destroying that layer preserves transferred or retained sprites, including their playback, bone bindings and modifiers\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBremoveSprite()\fP, \fBPart::attachSprite()\fP 
.RE
.PP

