.SS "deserialize (\fBDeserializer\fP deserializer)"

.PP
Restore Layer state or apply an incremental update\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdeserializer\fP Reader positioned at a record written by \fBSpriteLayer::serialize()\fP\&. An initial record restores sprites, independent/authored Parts, shared artwork, order, transforms and active state into an empty or populated Layer\&. Loading validates records and resources before replacing the existing collection, including mount endpoint, cycle and duplicate-owner checks\&. Old sprites retained by script are detached; new bodies join the destination solver after validation\&. Tween channels are rebound to the destination Layer, including zoom\&.
.RE
.PP
The Layer keeps its \fBPort\fP, application event handlers and caller-selected serialization flags\&. Its saved identities and state replace their previous values\&. A record/resource validation error leaves the existing Layer collection and state intact; discard the failed reader\&. Incremental updates modify existing sprites and require matching identities/order\&. They are not staged scene replacement\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Call outside animation modifiers and a physics solve\&. The shared physical world is not recreated; configure its gravity and damping in the application\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSpriteLayer::serialize()\fP, \fBSpriteLayer::setSerializationFlags()\fP 
.RE
.PP

