.SS "removeSprite (\fBSprite\fP oldSprite)"

.PP
Remove a \fBSprite\fP and its mounted descendants from this layer\&. Preserves mount relationships and layer-coordinate transforms\&. Retained groups can be animated off-layer and added to another layer\&. Removing a mounted child independently throws; detach it first\&. Sprites outside this layer are unchanged\&. Physics bodies leave the shared solver and retain their state for basic integration; root constraints and physical animation rigs are disconnected\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIoldSprite\fP The root of the group to remove\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Native callers must retain the host with addRef()/release() to keep it alive after removal\&. JavaScript handles retain automatically\&. Removal from a locked physics callback is deferred until the solve ends\&. Animation modifiers cannot change layer membership\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBaddSprite()\fP, \fBPart::detachSprite()\fP, \fBremoveAllSprites()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "serialize (\fBSerializer\fP serializer)"

.PP
Save selected Layer state and its ordered sprites\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIserializer\fP Destination writer; select its resource mode before writing\&. \fBsetSerializationFlags()\fP selects state\&. The default \fR\fBpdg\&.ser_Full\fP\fP includes Layer draw transforms, initial identities, frame artwork, playback, programmed tweens, root and \fBPart\fP \fBPhysicsBody\fP state and active drives\&. Remaining Layer fade completion delays are stored in seconds\&. Shared images are written once and use the writer's embedded-resource or external-reference policy\&.
.RE
.PP
Updates with \fR\fBser_Animations\fP\fP (including \fR\fBser_Update\fP\fP) transfer sampled local \fBPart\fP transforms, reflection, constant movement and scheduled animations by \fBPart\fP ID\&. They preserve existing \fBPart\fP identities, parent links and artwork\&. This includes poses already solved by \fBPart\fP IK\&. The receiver can stop Layer animations and disable collisions to display only the received state\&. \fBPart\fP creation/removal, reparenting, artwork changes, IK controller configuration and \fBPart\fP body/constraint state require another initial snapshot; incremental \fBPart\fP records are not full physics checkpoints\&. A changed \fBPart\fP ID set is rejected\&.

.PP
Independent Parts retain IDs/names, parent links, transforms, tweens and shared Image/Drawing content\&. Parent links resolve before body publication\&. Nested \fBDrawing\fP geometry/attributes are embedded; referenced images use the save policy\&. Rigid mounts retain their mounting \fBPart\fP, child \fBSprite\fP, sampled child grip frame, error/held pose and nested relationships\&. Children retain their independent layer draw order\&. Mount links resolve after all Sprite/Part identities exist; nonphysical and kinematic children retain the same ownership and command restrictions\&.

.PP
\fBDrawing\fP colors and image transparency colors use eight-bit channels, with opaque alpha omitted\&. Floating-point colors can change by less than one channel step (1/255) when restored\&. \fBImage\fP pixel data is preserved exactly\&. \fBDrawing\fP geometry, pixel-space attributes (including thickness, text size, offsets and transform translation), and image subsections use the compact coordinate serializers\&. These can discard a fractional remainder smaller than 0\&.001 per encoded coordinate component\&. Rectangles encode their origin and size, so those small errors can accumulate at the opposite edge\&. Physics state, collision geometry, constraint anchors, IK inputs and Sprite/Part transforms retain their existing floating-point precision\&.

.PP
Packed boolean flags omit default values and absent payloads\&. Repeated images, \fBDrawing\fP storage and imported animation assets use shared object references within the same serializer stream\&. This preserves shared identity and avoids writing the same resource again; independently created objects remain distinct\&.

.PP
Imported SCML animations retain their shared model, selected entity/clip, floating-point playback time, pause/events, character maps, reference pose, bone overrides, blends and interrupted transitions\&. Bone-, artwork- and socket-bound Parts resolve against the restored rig\&. Built-in rig IK modifiers and retained \fBDrawing\fP registrations preserve their IDs, options and enabled state\&. Animation colliders continue following the restored pose\&.

.PP
Complete saves embed the imported document and its images and can load without the source files\&. Embedded XML is compressed losslessly with zlib when that makes it smaller; decompression is automatic\&. Documents are limited to 64 MiB before compression, and corrupt payloads or mismatched lengths cause a load error\&. External-reference saves omit the XML, resolve the original document path and verify that its contents have not changed; images use the selected resource policy\&. Missing or changed dependencies cause a load error\&.

.PP
Initial records preserve \fBCollider\fP shapes and shape IDs, frame/animation-source options, material overrides, collision filters, sensor/enabled state and contact-event opt-in\&. Compound-body associations, all \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP types, linked IK limits and active physical \fBPart\fP IK controllers resolve after all owners exist\&. Captured IK offsets and sampled drives survive; offsets are not recaptured from a deformed pose\&. Geometry is stored in both resource modes; frame images follow the resource policy\&. Restored colliders receive new process-wide IDs\&.

.PP
Callback collision filters/handlers are rejected; reinstall application handlers after loading\&. Solver contact caches and pending contact events are not saved, so loading rebuilds contacts and can produce new Begin events\&. A resumed simulation is not guaranteed to be bit-for-bit identical to an uninterrupted one\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Initial saves support frame-based and imported \fBSprite\fP collections with Parts, colliders, constraints, physical \fBPart\fP IK and rigid mounts\&. Active imported physical rigs, older attachSprite() associations, modifier/drawing callbacks, custom easing/helpers, \fBFont\fP attributes, custom \fBDrawing\fP implementations and links to other layers are rejected\&. \fBDrawing\fP content requires a GUI-capable build\&. \fBPort\fP assignment, event handlers and the shared physics world's gravity/damping configuration belong to the receiving application\&. Discard the writer after a save error\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
// layer contains sprites with no unsupported graph associations\&.
const writer = new pdg\&.Serializer();
writer\&.setResourceMode(pdg\&.serialization_Complete);
layer\&.setSerializationFlags(pdg\&.ser_Full);
layer\&.serialize(writer);
const reader = new pdg\&.Deserializer();
reader\&.setDataPtr(writer\&.getDataPtr());
const restored = pdg\&.createSpriteLayer();
restored\&.deserialize(reader);
// Use restored, then pdg\&.cleanupLayer(restored) when finished\&.
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSpriteLayer::deserialize()\fP, \fBSpriteLayer::getSerializedSize()\fP, \fBSerializer::setResourceMode()\fP 
.RE
.PP

